@@ -47,6 +47,15 @@ All tables use UUIDs (UUIDv7 format, base36-encoded as 25-char strings):
 - Fixtures are always "older" than runtime records
 - `.first`/`.last` work correctly in tests
 
+### Notification Emails
+
+Notifications are not emailed one by one. Each person's notifications are bundled into time windows and one email is sent per window (`Notification::EmailWindow`):
+
+- The frequency is chosen per person with `bundle_email_frequency` on their settings: `never`, `every_few_hours`, `daily` or `weekly`.
+- The clock starts when the first notification of a window lands; the window closes once that frequency has passed.
+- Notifications that arrive late belong to the window that has already opened, so windows never overlap.
+- `Notification::EmailWindowJob` delivers the windows that are due. It is scheduled in `config/recurring.yml`.
+
 ### Background Jobs (Solid Queue)
 
 Database-backed job queue (no Redis):
